        }
      ],
      "message": "doc: document ZMQ notification asynchrony and RPC synchronization\n\nNote in zmq.md that notifications are dispatched asynchronously after the\nnode's state is updated, so a subscriber may observe the node ahead of a\nnotification it just received (e.g. getbestblockhash returning a later block\nthan the one announced via hashblock). Advise treating notifications as a\ntrigger to re-query the node, and clarify that message ordering is guaranteed\nonly within a topic, not across the ZMQ, -*notify, and RPC interfaces.\n\nThis addresses part of #14278.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "fernandguil",
        "email": "39845628+fernandguil@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-08-28T03:20:59Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "fernandguil",
        "email": "39845628+fernandguil@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-08-28T01:30:20Z"
      },
